   "en": {
    "headline": "Google launches Gemini 4 Hydrogen, its fast model for coding and agents, and Orchestrator mode",
    "summary_short": "Google launches Gemini 4 Hydrogen, a fast model for coding and agents that beats Gemini 4 Argon on the Artificial Analysis index. With it, Gemini 4 reaches everyone: the Gemini app, Search and the API.",
    "summary_long": "Hydrogen is the fast model in the Gemini 4 family, built to write code, run tests and chain agent tasks. At its default reasoning level it scores 51 on the Artificial Analysis index, one point above Gemini 4 Argon, and 54 at the highest level. Compared with Gemini 3.8 Flash, it finishes tasks 2.5 times faster and rises from 18.2% to 57% on Terminal-Bench 4.1. It costs $1.50 per million input tokens and $7.50 per million output tokens. It is already the default model in Search's AI Mode.\n\nGoogle is also launching Orchestrator in Antigravity, its agentic coding environment. It splits a single session between models: Carbon plans and handles the hard parts, and Hydrogen writes and tests the code. On Terminal-Bench it comes close to Carbon's success rate while using 24% less quota and running 19% faster. All figures come from Google.",
    "unconfirmed_claims": []
   },
